- *Skill checks:*
  - *Investigate D2:* Build the timeline. The pattern is stark: every
    victim was alone or in a small group, every disappearance is in the
    northeast, and the frequency is increasing. Whatever is doing this is
    getting hungrier --- or bolder.
  - *Influence D3:* The reeve opens up about the toll on the community.
    People are afraid to leave the walls; the forager economy is
    collapsing. She is grateful someone is finally taking this seriously.
    (Mbazân's lane --- Influence 7.)

== Lead 2: Dashek, the Survivor

Dashek was half of the first patrol sent out --- the other half was
Sergeant Vazhan. Dashek did not see what happened: one moment Vazhan was
there, the next he was not. Dashek found signs of a brief struggle and no
body, searched until dark, and has not slept properly since.

- *What he provides without a check:* the place where Vazhan vanished ---
  a fold of foothills northeast of the village, where the Weald thins and
  the Fog draws close. This is the party's starting point. *Do not make
  the party roll for this.*

- *Skill checks:*
  - *Influence D2:* Get him talking properly. He wants to help but is
    drowning in guilt; a sympathetic approach works better than a
    demanding one. He describes the terrain in useful detail --- landmarks,
    the creek crossing, the game trails (this earns the *preparation
    bonus* in the tracking challenge below).
  - *Awareness D3:* Notice what he is not saying: Vazhan was his sergeant
    and his friend, and Dashek ran when the silence got too loud. He has
    been telling himself he searched thoroughly. He did not.

#note[
  *If Ushtâng is in play:* Vazhan was Ushtâng's friend too --- that is why
  Ushtâng is here. Let the two of them have a beat. Dashek can tell
  Ushtâng what the official reports would not: Vazhan's halberd was gone
  with him, and there was no blood. Ushtâng's player now has a name to
  carry into Scene 2 --- do not foreshadow further.
]

== Optional Lead: Ibbeh's Customer

If the party asks around the market about strangers or unusual purchases
(*Investigate D3* to find the right person), they are pointed to Ibbeh, a
dry-goods trader with a long memory.

She remembers a remarkable customer from about half a year ago: tall,
Mirror features --- the fey shimmer of an Echo --- polite, spoke in
measured sentences. Bought in bulk: glassware, reagents, heavy sealed
containers. Asked odd questions about the local Fog. Always left
northeast. Stopped coming perhaps six months ago.

#note[
  This is colour now and confirmation later --- Sennakht will put a name
  to the description in Scene 3. If the party skips this lead, nothing is
  lost. If time is short, cut it.
]

== Into the Field: The Tracking Challenge

Dashek's directions give the party the right _area_, not the right
_location_. The journey northeast takes half a day on foot; the last
stretch is a search.

#flavor[
  The forest changes as you move northeast. The canopy thins. The
  underbrush grows sparser but stranger --- pale shoots, fungi that should
  not grow this far from the Fog. The birdsong stops before you notice it
  has stopped. The air takes on a faint chemical tang that does not belong
  to any forest.
]

The party makes a short series of group checks to find the ravine. Each
stretch represents a section of the Weald that must be searched or
reasoned through.

*Number of stretches:* Start with 2. Each failed check adds 1 stretch (to
a maximum of 3 total). Each success clears 1.

*Available checks (each stretch, the party picks an approach and a lead
roller; others may assist):*
- *Awareness D3:* Read the terrain --- broken branches at a consistent
  height, undergrowth trampled in a line, pale fungi clustering along
  disturbed soil. Something has passed this way many times. (Kalariyar's
  lane --- Awareness 7.)
- *Investigate D3:* Reason out the disposal logic. Whoever is behind this
  needs somewhere screened from observation, far from Keshto, near the
  Fog boundary. That narrows the search to ravines and depressions in one
  corridor of the Weald.
- *Stamina D4:* Brute persistence --- push through rough terrain and
  Fog-headache to walk the grid when cleverness fails.

*Preparation bonus:* If the party got Dashek's detailed directions
(the Influence D2 above), reduce all DCs by 1. Say so out loud --- this
is the lesson: _talking to people before you leave makes the wilderness
easier._

*Complications on failure (pick one per failed stretch):*
- A wrong drainage channel costs an hour; the party will reach the ravine
  at dusk. (This is atmospheric, not punitive --- and kind to Kalariyar,
  whose Shade eyes dislike daylight.)
- A loose scree slope: the character who led the check makes an
  *Athletics D3* or takes 3 damage and arrives at the bottom Prone.
- The party crosses a Fog-Touched Beast's hunting ground. In Scene 2,
  the beasts are present from round 1 instead of arriving on round 2.

#note[
  *Pacing:* 5--10 minutes of real time. Describe each stretch briefly ---
  a fork in the terrain, a moment of doubt --- call for the check, narrate
  the result, and move on. Two successes and they are there.
]
